ecomment-1846791695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/5180","id":1846791695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBCRpgs5uE84P","user":{"login":"metcoder95","id":10200776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjAwNzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10200776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95","html_url":"https://github.com/metcoder95","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-08T08:55:30Z","updated_at":"2023-12-08T08:55:30Z","body":"👋 \r\n\r\n>I tried debugging the issue and it appears to be related to this line ([main/lib/server.js#L178](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/main/lib/server.js?rgh-link-date=2023-11-30T11%3A39%3A14Z#L178)) where Fastify attaches a onClose handler that tries to close the secondary server without calling any preClose hooks unlike the primary server ([main/fastify.js#L433](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/main/fastify.js?rgh-link-date=2023-11-30T11%3A39%3A14Z#L433)). This means that @fastify/websocket is unable to shutdown the sockets appropriately leading the secondary server to stall the close process indefinitely.\r\n\r\nThe `preClose` hook should not be called twice, AFAIC, the order seems to be correct. `preClose` will be called just before closing the first, and subsequently, the secondary server. Trying to run it in both will cause a duplicate of running hooks; unless that's the desired behaviour, here we will change the experience.\r\n\r\nI'm guessing here that `websocket` might not be aware of the existence of the two servers. I can see an explicit detach `upgrade` event from server A but not B.\r\n\r\nHave you tried providing your own `preClose` cb?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1846791695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"metcoder95","id":10200776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjAwNzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10200776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95","html_url":"https://github.com/metcoder95","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1847151523","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify/fastify/issues/5180#issuecomment-1847151523","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/5180","id":1847151523,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBCRpgs5uGUuj","user":{"login":"kingston","id":339308,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTMwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/339308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston","html_url":"https://github.com/kingston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-08T13:16:55Z","updated_at":"2023-12-08T13:16:55Z","body":"> 👋\r\n> \r\n> > I tried debugging the issue and it appears to be related to this line ([main/lib/server.js#L178](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/main/lib/server.js?rgh-link-date=2023-11-30T11%3A39%3A14Z#L178)) where Fastify attaches a onClose handler that tries to close the secondary server without calling any preClose hooks unlike the primary server ([main/fastify.js#L433](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/main/fastify.js?rgh-link-date=2023-11-30T11%3A39%3A14Z#L433)). This means that @fastify/websocket is unable to shutdown the sockets appropriately leading the secondary server to stall the close process indefinitely.\r\n> \r\n> The `preClose` hook should not be called twice, AFAIC, the order seems to be correct. `preClose` will be called just before closing the first, and subsequently, the secondary server. Trying to run it in both will cause a duplicate of running hooks; unless that's the desired behaviour, here we will change the experience.\r\n> \r\n> I'm guessing here that `websocket` might not be aware of the existence of the two servers. I can see an explicit detach `upgrade` event from server A but not B.\r\n> \r\n> Have you tried providing your own `preClose` cb?\r\n\r\nThe issue is that the global preClose hooks are called after the secondary server runs its onClose handler. Therefore, there's nothing to hook into before the secondary server calls onClose which hangs indefinitely since there are open websockets. I think what should happen is:\r\n1) preClose hooks\r\n2) close primary server\r\n3) close secondary server\r\n\r\nBut what is happening appears to be (based on debug statements):\r\n1) close secondary server\r\n2) preClose hooks\r\n3) close primary server\r\n\r\nI can take a look at the code to see if a quick PR can be made but less familiar with how the whole hook system works. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1847151523/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kingston","id":339308,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTMwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/339308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston","html_url":"https://github.com/kingston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kingston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1847715310","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify/fastify/issues/5180#issuecomment-1847715310","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/5180","id":1847715310,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBCRpgs5uIeXu","user":{"login":"metcoder95","id":10200776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjAwNzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10200776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95","html_url":"https://github.com/metcoder95","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-08T19:36:25Z","updated_at":"2023-12-08T19:36:25Z","body":"Yeah, it makes sense now.\r\nFeel free to open a PR, we can provide some guidance there 👍 \r\n\r\nI'd recommend you take a look at this function call: https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/b9336a3f3979f0d024a73222e193d1317bafc69a/fastify.js#L433-L452\r\n\r\nAnd seek if there's a way of closing the secondary just after the hooks has run (when is basically when the CB submitted to the `hook runner` gets called).\r\nAs hooks can be asynchronous, most likely we reach this line https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/b9336a3f3979f0d024a73222e193d1317bafc69a/fastify.js#L459 before even finishing the execution of all the hooks, leading to this problem.","author_association":"MEMBE